0025: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0026:     """
0027:     Extend the blue square up-left and the red square down-right along their diagonals to the grid edge.
0028: 
0029:     Input structure
0030:     - The grid has a black background.
0031:     - There is exactly one blue 2x2 square and exactly one red 2x2 square.
0032:     - The diagonal ray beyond each active corner is clear background until it leaves the grid.
0033: 
0034:     Rule
0035:     - Keep the input pixels unchanged.
0036:     - From the blue square's top-left corner, paint a blue diagonal ray in the up-left direction.
0037:     - From the red square's bottom-right corner, paint a red diagonal ray in the down-right direction.
0038:     - Each ray stops only when the next step would leave the grid.
